-- title:
--   Clifford hierarchy $C_{k+1}$ (level $k$): $C_1$ Pauli, $C_k=\{U\mid UC_1U^\dagger\subseteq C_{k-1}\}$
-- statement:
--   On $n$ qubits the Clifford hierarchy is defined recursively: $C_1$ is the Pauli group $\mathcal P_n$ (tensor products of $I,X,Y,Z$ with overall phases $\pm1,\pm i$), and for $k\ge2$
--
--   $$C_k=\{\,U \text{ unitary}\mid U P U^\dagger\in C_{k-1}\ \text{for every } P\in C_1\,\}.$$
--
--   $C_2$ is the Clifford group, the unitaries mapping Pauli operators to Pauli operators under conjugation; $C_3$ (Eq. (2)) contains the Toffoli and $\pi/8$ gates.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The Lean index is shifted by one: `cliffordLevel n k` is $C_{k+1}$, so level $0$ is the Pauli group and level $1$ the Clifford group. Elements are members of `Matrix.unitaryGroup`, where $U^{-1}=U^\dagger$. The Pauli group is `QAlgorithms.pauliGroup n`, with phases $\pm1,\pm i$; the p. 2 phrase "with overall sign ±1" is not closed under products, and the levels $C_k$, $k\ge2$, do not depend on this choice.
-- source:
--   Gottesman, Chuang, Quantum teleportation is a universal computational primitive, arXiv:quant-ph/9908010v1, §II, p. 3 (C1, C2), Eq. (2) (C3), and §III Conclusion, p. 3 (Ck ≡ {U|UC1U† ⊆ Ck−1})

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Defs_Basic
import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Defs_QECC

namespace TeleportGates.Ck

open QAlgorithms

/-- **The Clifford hierarchy: `cliffordLevel n k` is the paper's `C_{k+1}`.**
Gottesman, Chuang, *Quantum teleportation is a universal computational primitive*,
arXiv:quant-ph/9908010v1, §II, p. 3: "Let C1 represent the Pauli group.
C2, the Clifford group, will be the set of gates which map Pauli operators into Pauli operators
under conjugation." Eq. (2), p. 3: "C3 ≡ {U | UC1U† ⊆ C2}." §III, p. 3: "an infinite family of
gates, Ck ≡ {U|UC1U† ⊆ Ck−1}".

On `n` qubits, `cliffordLevel n 0` is the Pauli group `P_n` (`QAlgorithms.pauliGroup n`,
generated by the tensor products of `I, X, Y, Z` with phases `±1, ±i`), and
`cliffordLevel n (k+1)` is the set of unitaries `U` with `U P U† ∈ cliffordLevel n k` for every
`P` in the Pauli group.

**Formalization Note.** The index is shifted by one: `cliffordLevel n 0 = C₁` (Pauli group),
`cliffordLevel n 1 = C₂` (Clifford group), `cliffordLevel n 2 = C₃`; there is no `C₀`. Elements
are unitary matrices (`Matrix.unitaryGroup`), where `U⁻¹ = U†`. The Pauli group carries the
phases `±1, ±i`: the p. 2 parenthetical "with overall sign ±1" is not closed under products
(`XZ = −iY`); for `k ≥ 1` the level is the same under either reading, since conjugation by `U`
fixes scalars. -/
noncomputable def cliffordLevel (n : ℕ) : ℕ → Set (Matrix.unitaryGroup (Qubits n) ℂ)
  | 0 => (pauliGroup n : Set (Matrix.unitaryGroup (Qubits n) ℂ))
  | k + 1 => {U | ∀ P ∈ pauliGroup n, U * P * U⁻¹ ∈ cliffordLevel n k}

end TeleportGates.Ck


